## Reading this result while the data are still coming in

The interval and p-value above come from a confidence sequence: they hold at every sample size at
once, so the result may be read after every observation, and a decision to stop because it looks
good does not inflate the false-positive rate. The fixed-horizon test in each table is shown only
for comparison; it is valid just once, at a sample size fixed in advance, and peeking at it
inflates false positives (see `validation/failure_gallery/04_peeking.py`). The price is a wider
interval: the sequence is tuned to be tightest around the planned sample size.
